WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.812
1Password Security

00:00:01.624 --> 00:00:02.378
Incident

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.608
1Password has disclosed

00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:05.763
a security incident

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:06.754
and published an

00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:07.355
update on its

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:07.851
blog

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:08.838
We have triggered

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:09.522
a rotation of

00:00:09.393 --> 00:00:10.654
all credentials which

00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:11.067
may have been

00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:11.668
exposed

00:00:11.799 --> 00:00:12.482
and there is

00:00:12.294 --> 00:00:13.426
no impact to

00:00:13.237 --> 00:00:14.852
1Password’s services

00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:16.645
availability or product

00:00:16.457 --> 00:00:17.211
security

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.351
On November 19, 2026

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:22.592
1Password began investigating

00:00:22.404 --> 00:00:23.594
indications that an

00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:24.939
attacker gained access

00:00:24.751 --> 00:00:25.788
to an employee’s

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.073
corporate GitHub account

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:28.733
During this incident

00:00:28.545 --> 00:00:29.099
there were a

00:00:28.911 --> 00:00:29.913
small number of

00:00:29.724 --> 00:00:30.573
users in this

00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:30.915
state

00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:31.717
who have been

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:33.049
specifically notified

00:00:33.582 --> 00:00:34.596
Full story on

00:00:34.407 --> 00:00:35.303
the dashboard
